    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "11680db0-67b4-5752-84da-0d7597ffa0b7",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$H=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$J=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$L=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $H$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $J$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 3 columns.\n\n- $L$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 3 columns.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ is a diagonal matrix.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
