    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4fb98a06-ac68-5e3c-8cb4-6af6dd4c51ad",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are diagonal matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$Y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $S$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 4 rows and 2 columns.\n\n- $R$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $Y$ is a diagonal matrix. It is square and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\nTherefore, only $R$ and $Y$ are diagonal matrices.",
